1
00:00:24,024 --> 00:00:25,158
FREELANCE SURGEON
MICHIKO DAIMON

2
00:00:25,225 --> 00:00:26,259
I have

3
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:35,335
no money!

4
00:00:49,582 --> 00:00:53,653
A house sitting in the middle of nowhere!

5
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:01,294
Hello?

6
00:01:01,628 --> 00:01:03,129
Excuse me!

7
00:01:10,470 --> 00:01:12,772
Excuse me. Is this your house?

8
00:01:15,642 --> 00:01:17,210
Will you share these with me?

9
00:01:17,310 --> 00:01:19,112
I doubt I'll make a mistake.

10
00:01:19,779 --> 00:01:21,581
- Okay.
- Really?

11
00:01:31,224 --> 00:01:32,492
Magnificent!

12
00:01:34,027 --> 00:01:35,328
Wow, nice!

13
00:01:37,163 --> 00:01:38,298
Where are you from?

14
00:01:39,432 --> 00:01:41,701
I just came here from Brazil.

15
00:01:42,202 --> 00:01:44,904
Where did you learn Portuguese?

16
00:01:46,072 --> 00:01:47,740
I've lived all over the place.

17
00:01:48,741 --> 00:01:50,410
Then we're alike.

18
00:01:51,044 --> 00:01:53,213
Are you a chef?

19
00:01:53,646 --> 00:01:55,415
Or maybe a fishmonger?

20
00:01:57,383 --> 00:01:58,685
That's about right.

21
00:01:58,785 --> 00:02:00,620
I sometimes do dissection shows.

22
00:02:01,387 --> 00:02:03,490
I would like to see that.

23
00:02:05,492 --> 00:02:06,526
Eat up.

24
00:02:06,626 --> 00:02:09,696
Thank you.

25
00:02:14,934 --> 00:02:17,337
As you can see, these past ten years,

26
00:02:17,403 --> 00:02:20,607
our debts have increased
to over twenty billion yen.

27
00:02:20,707 --> 00:02:24,511
Next fiscal year, we predict that
we'll fall behind on our debts.

28
00:02:25,311 --> 00:02:26,980
We'll go bankrupt in a year?

29
00:02:27,046 --> 00:02:28,781
The great Totei University Hospital?

30
00:02:28,882 --> 00:02:30,683
We're drowning in debt.

31
00:02:30,783 --> 00:02:32,252
Now's my chance.

32
00:02:32,352 --> 00:02:36,489
I've gathered the satellite hospital
directors here today

33
00:02:36,689 --> 00:02:40,894
to get your thoughts on
the financial crisis

34
00:02:41,161 --> 00:02:42,996
that Totei University Hospital...

35
00:02:43,062 --> 00:02:44,264
HOSPITAL DIRECTOR
SHIGEKATSU HIRUMA

36
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:45,832
...finds itself in.

37
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:50,970
What should we prioritize?

38
00:02:51,571 --> 00:02:53,373
I would like your insights.

39
00:02:56,643 --> 00:03:01,047
Director of Lake Mashu Satellite
Hospital 39 in Hokkaido,

40
00:03:01,548 --> 00:03:05,818
Makoto Ebina, let me have your thoughts.

41
00:03:06,085 --> 00:03:07,020
It's Takashi.

42
00:03:08,454 --> 00:03:09,422
Excuse me.

43
00:03:11,090 --> 00:03:14,561
What I believe we need in order to
overcome this crisis is

44
00:03:15,929 --> 00:03:18,898
change and challenge.

45
00:03:25,171 --> 00:03:27,840
- Shut up.
- Yes, sir.

46
00:03:31,945 --> 00:03:34,414
Japanese fish are too weak.

47
00:03:35,148 --> 00:03:40,153
At this rate, they'll be gobbled up
by invasive species.

48
00:03:40,653 --> 00:03:43,389
That's why I eat black bass,

49
00:03:43,456 --> 00:03:44,891
to protect Japanese fish.

50
00:03:45,825 --> 00:03:46,893
Is that right?

51
00:03:47,927 --> 00:03:50,029
- Can I have another caipirinha?
- Sure.

52
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:57,403
What did you come way up here
into the mountains for?

53
00:03:58,071 --> 00:04:02,242
I heard there's a hot spring
you can use for free out here.

54
00:04:02,342 --> 00:04:05,044
But I got lost and got separated
from my companion.

55
00:04:07,347 --> 00:04:09,983
This is so relaxing.

56
00:04:10,383 --> 00:04:12,685
Where the heck did Michiko go?

57
00:04:13,519 --> 00:04:14,454
Right?

58
00:04:16,456 --> 00:04:19,259
But since I got to have these
delicious black bass,

59
00:04:19,792 --> 00:04:21,160
I feel lucky!

60
00:04:21,227 --> 00:04:24,897
I'm also glad I made
such an interesting friend.

61
00:04:25,465 --> 00:04:27,000
Let's dance together!

62
00:04:31,471 --> 00:04:33,306
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

63
00:04:38,177 --> 00:04:39,279
Samejima...

64
00:04:45,251 --> 00:04:46,352
Samejima!

65
00:04:51,391 --> 00:04:52,425
Are you all right?

66
00:04:52,492 --> 00:04:53,493
Hang in there!

67
00:05:02,869 --> 00:05:04,170
You're a doctor?

68
00:05:04,270 --> 00:05:05,471
Help me.

69
00:05:05,705 --> 00:05:06,973
Help me.

70
00:05:11,177 --> 00:05:13,279
There's no blood flowing to
his left forearm.

71
00:05:13,379 --> 00:05:17,050
It will take two hours
for a rescue team to get here.

72
00:05:17,250 --> 00:05:18,818
By then, his arm will undergo necrosis,

73
00:05:19,018 --> 00:05:20,520
and he'll suffer crush syndrome.

74
00:05:31,864 --> 00:05:32,965
What are you doing?

75
00:05:33,066 --> 00:05:34,701
I'll put you back together. Deal with it.

76
00:05:34,767 --> 00:05:35,968
You'll die unless I do this.

77
00:05:36,069 --> 00:05:37,170
Don't.

78
00:05:38,604 --> 00:05:39,839
Don't!

79
00:05:40,707 --> 00:05:43,009
I never fail.

80
00:05:48,781 --> 00:05:52,251
<i>This is the story of
a maverick female doctor.</i>

81
00:05:53,052 --> 00:05:57,623
<i>In 2019, the ivory towers are
completely crumbling.</i>

82
00:05:58,825 --> 00:06:02,662
<i>Japan's university hospitals have
fallen into tremendous debt.</i>

83
00:06:02,929 --> 00:06:05,298
<i>Lifesaving medical treatment</i>

84
00:06:05,765 --> 00:06:09,502
<i>has entered the era of
financial jungle law.</i>

85
00:06:09,569 --> 00:06:11,404
I have found a silver bullet

86
00:06:11,504 --> 00:06:14,507
for the financial crisis that
Totei University Hospital

87
00:06:14,907 --> 00:06:16,175
is facing.

88
00:06:17,243 --> 00:06:18,745
30 BILLION YEN INVESTMENT

89
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:26,986
I succeeded in receiving investment
from a foreign medical fund.

90
00:06:28,221 --> 00:06:30,256
The amount I got was...

91
00:06:30,656 --> 00:06:32,658
- Thirty billion yen.
- Thirty billion yen.

92
00:06:38,865 --> 00:06:44,604
Also, the manager and lead advisor
of this fund,

93
00:06:45,104 --> 00:06:48,241
I have invited him

94
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:52,078
to restructure Totei University Hospital.

95
00:06:52,145 --> 00:06:53,813
FOREIGN MEDICAL FUND

96
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:57,950
I think you could call him this century's

97
00:06:58,384 --> 00:07:01,320
greatest savior.

98
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:05,057
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

99
00:07:05,491 --> 00:07:06,659
Thank you.

100
00:07:11,964 --> 00:07:13,366
Way out here?

101
00:07:13,599 --> 00:07:15,201
SURGEON
HIDEKI KAJI

102
00:07:15,501 --> 00:07:17,036
TOTEI UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

103
00:07:19,572 --> 00:07:21,174
It's even further from here?

104
00:07:24,377 --> 00:07:25,478
Over here!

105
00:07:25,778 --> 00:07:26,879
Over here!

106
00:07:26,979 --> 00:07:30,383
Michiko Daimon is way out here?

107
00:07:31,250 --> 00:07:32,518
Hurry!

108
00:07:33,386 --> 00:07:34,987
Why the heck are you out here?

109
00:07:35,054 --> 00:07:37,290
Shut up!
Get this patient to the hospital quickly.

110
00:07:42,462 --> 00:07:45,298
Don't tell me you did it with this!

111
00:07:45,364 --> 00:07:48,401
I'll attach his forearm wherever
I can perform emergency surgery.

112
00:07:48,501 --> 00:07:50,303
Did you do this to him with this?

113
00:07:50,369 --> 00:07:51,838
- Shut up!
- Okay.

114
00:07:58,945 --> 00:08:02,215
That's a magnificent skill you have.

115
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:04,784
Who are you, sir?

116
00:08:04,851 --> 00:08:05,751
Farewell.

117
00:08:06,185 --> 00:08:08,054
Let's meet again,

118
00:08:08,921 --> 00:08:10,823
miss doctor that never fails.

119
00:08:12,024 --> 00:08:13,025
Farewell.

120
00:08:13,793 --> 00:08:15,528
TOTEI UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

121
00:08:30,810 --> 00:08:32,612
The black ships have arrived.

122
00:08:43,856 --> 00:08:47,627
Welcome, our savior, Nicholas Tange.

123
00:08:48,861 --> 00:08:50,096
Nicholas Tange?

124
00:08:50,429 --> 00:08:52,899
He's this century's greatest cost cutter.

125
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:55,301
Hello.

126
00:08:56,269 --> 00:08:57,870
It's nice to meet you.

127
00:08:58,704 --> 00:09:00,840
I have no idea what he's saying.

128
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:04,043
- Show him around!
- Yes, sir!

129
00:09:04,143 --> 00:09:06,345
- To the large meeting room!
- Yes, sir!

130
00:09:08,981 --> 00:09:10,650
How's your arm?

131
00:09:10,950 --> 00:09:13,286
See for yourself.

132
00:09:13,719 --> 00:09:15,388
Okay, what's first?

133
00:09:15,454 --> 00:09:16,889
I wonder what he's saying.

134
00:09:17,156 --> 00:09:19,492
He's probably criticizing us.

135
00:09:19,892 --> 00:09:22,061
Does anyone here speak Portuguese?

136
00:09:22,161 --> 00:09:23,729
You mean he's speaking Portuguese?

137
00:09:23,829 --> 00:09:26,132
If I could speak it,
I would give him a piece of my mind.

138
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:28,634
How could a cost cutter
without a medical license

139
00:09:28,701 --> 00:09:30,002
ever save a university hospital?

140
00:09:30,069 --> 00:09:31,170
There's no way!

141
00:09:38,978 --> 00:09:41,247
There isn't a business around
that I cannot save.

142
00:09:41,881 --> 00:09:42,982
That's a shock.

143
00:09:43,449 --> 00:09:45,685
So you can speak Japanese.

144
00:09:45,785 --> 00:09:48,688
Might I also add that
I may be an investor,

145
00:09:49,088 --> 00:09:51,524
but I have also obtained
a medical license.

146
00:09:51,724 --> 00:09:52,692
Seriously?

147
00:09:53,225 --> 00:09:57,663
<i>Meanwhile, this freelance
maverick doctor, who was never part of</i>

148
00:09:58,030 --> 00:10:01,667
<i>a university medical department,
showed up.</i>

149
00:10:02,868 --> 00:10:06,472
<i>This woman hates groups,</i>

150
00:10:06,839 --> 00:10:09,642
<i>authority, and restrictions.</i>

151
00:10:10,309 --> 00:10:13,546
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

152
00:10:13,779 --> 00:10:15,548
<i>are her weapons.</i>

153
00:10:16,182 --> 00:10:20,286
If you're a lifesaving doctor,
why did you become an investor?

154
00:10:20,519 --> 00:10:23,222
People die not just of disease
but of poverty too.

155
00:10:24,056 --> 00:10:26,726
Totei University Hospital is
on the verge of death.

156
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:29,862
It requires massive surgery immediately.

157
00:10:31,297 --> 00:10:33,432
It will bleed significantly
in this surgery

158
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,302
and undergo nearly unbearable pain.

159
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:40,840
But that's the only way
that it can survive.

160
00:10:44,910 --> 00:10:48,280
Believe in me and stick by my side.

161
00:10:50,182 --> 00:10:55,087
There isn't a business around
that I cannot save.

162
00:10:57,990 --> 00:11:00,259
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

163
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:04,330
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

164
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:23,382
- Ebina.
- Yes?

165
00:11:23,449 --> 00:11:26,686
Assistant Hospital Director Tange
still isn't here yet.

166
00:11:26,752 --> 00:11:28,320
Did you show him the way?

167
00:11:28,421 --> 00:11:29,989
Yes, I showed him here,

168
00:11:30,156 --> 00:11:31,791
but he disappeared before I knew it.

169
00:11:32,024 --> 00:11:32,858
What?

170
00:11:33,426 --> 00:11:35,528
Assistant Director Tange was
suddenly called away,

171
00:11:35,594 --> 00:11:36,829
so he'll miss this meeting.

172
00:11:36,896 --> 00:11:37,830
No way.

173
00:11:37,897 --> 00:11:39,598
I'm the new chief administrator, Samejima.

174
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:44,203
I will explain on behalf of
the Assistant Hospital Director.

175
00:11:44,303 --> 00:11:45,171
Okay.

176
00:11:45,271 --> 00:11:48,374
This is Totei University Hospital's
Rebirth Plan 2020.

177
00:11:48,641 --> 00:11:50,876
The key points are
selection and concentration.

178
00:11:50,943 --> 00:11:53,212
First, we'll eliminate
departments in the red

179
00:11:53,279 --> 00:11:54,980
and lay off unnecessary medical staff.

180
00:11:55,047 --> 00:11:58,517
Pediatrics, obstetrics,
and emergency care will be reduced,

181
00:11:58,584 --> 00:12:02,288
and 42 affiliated hospitals will be
consolidated nationwide.

182
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:04,457
Hold on a second here!

183
00:12:04,523 --> 00:12:07,259
We've been implementing
numerous cost-cutting measures.

184
00:12:07,359 --> 00:12:09,562
Medical devices and medications
have been severely curtailed.

185
00:12:09,628 --> 00:12:12,765
Any further cost cutting will cause
a reduction in the quality of treatment.

186
00:12:13,199 --> 00:12:15,701
- That's right!
- Hold on a minute!

187
00:12:16,001 --> 00:12:19,739
Totei University Hospital is
on the verge of collapse.

188
00:12:20,139 --> 00:12:23,542
A certain amount of
sacrifice is necessary.

189
00:12:24,110 --> 00:12:25,811
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

190
00:12:25,978 --> 00:12:27,880
- I can't hear you.
- Yes, sir!

191
00:12:27,947 --> 00:12:29,048
Thank you.

192
00:12:29,148 --> 00:12:33,152
The hospitals to be closed are
Oga Peninsula Satellite Hospital 18,

193
00:12:33,652 --> 00:12:36,455
- Kusatsu Satellite Hospital 25,
- Why us?

194
00:12:36,522 --> 00:12:38,524
Kasumigaura Satellite Hospital 29,

195
00:12:38,691 --> 00:12:40,726
Mount Yoro Satellite Hospital 31,

196
00:12:40,860 --> 00:12:42,762
Yazu Satellite Hospital 36,

197
00:12:42,928 --> 00:12:45,164
Alps Satellite Hospital 37,

198
00:12:45,297 --> 00:12:47,833
- Sado Island Satellite Hospital 38...
- Don't worry, everyone.

199
00:12:47,900 --> 00:12:50,102
I'll make sure you all have jobs.

200
00:12:50,169 --> 00:12:52,138
Lake Mashu Satellite Hospital 39.

201
00:12:52,204 --> 00:12:54,106
Me too?

202
00:12:54,173 --> 00:12:55,841
- You're kidding!
- On what basis?

203
00:12:55,941 --> 00:12:57,743
We're not in the red!

204
00:12:57,810 --> 00:13:00,613
Instead of us,
close Satellite Hospital 16 first!

205
00:13:00,679 --> 00:13:03,983
- Darn you! You traitor!
- Hold on here!

206
00:13:04,283 --> 00:13:06,752
Quit making me repeat myself!

207
00:13:07,052 --> 00:13:11,590
Without massive reforms,
Totei University Hospital will fail.

208
00:13:12,458 --> 00:13:13,526
Get it through your heads!

209
00:13:14,293 --> 00:13:15,528
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

210
00:13:15,628 --> 00:13:18,697
I will now introduce the new leaders
of the business streamlining.

211
00:13:18,898 --> 00:13:22,935
Director of Next-Generation
Intelligent Surgery,

212
00:13:23,002 --> 00:13:24,370
Professor Kazuma Ushio.

213
00:13:25,538 --> 00:13:27,006
Welcome.

214
00:13:30,442 --> 00:13:32,812
I'm Professor Ushio.
It's nice to meet you all.

215
00:13:33,279 --> 00:13:34,947
TOTEI

216
00:13:35,014 --> 00:13:38,217
Incompetent doctors will be
replaced by AI.

217
00:13:38,450 --> 00:13:39,518
Are you kidding me?

218
00:13:41,387 --> 00:13:44,190
Director of Next-Generation
Genome Oncology,

219
00:13:44,256 --> 00:13:45,224
Professor Mari Hamachi.

220
00:13:47,259 --> 00:13:48,294
Welcome.

221
00:13:49,762 --> 00:13:51,463
I'm Professor Hamachi.

222
00:13:51,530 --> 00:13:55,868
We will no longer need surgeons
who just want to cut people open.

223
00:13:56,001 --> 00:13:59,471
Study hard and follow my lead.

224
00:13:59,839 --> 00:14:01,574
Hey...

225
00:14:03,309 --> 00:14:07,279
Director of Next-Generation
Ultra-Minimally Invasive Surgery,

226
00:14:07,746 --> 00:14:08,881
Dr. Hideki Kaji.

227
00:14:09,181 --> 00:14:10,349
- What?
- What?

228
00:14:10,416 --> 00:14:11,650
Yes, sir.

229
00:14:14,386 --> 00:14:15,855
Hold on!

230
00:14:15,988 --> 00:14:19,225
Why is Kaji a director?
He's not even a professor!

231
00:14:19,291 --> 00:14:20,726
Former Director Ebina,

232
00:14:21,427 --> 00:14:24,029
I'm sorry to hear about
Satellite Hospital 39.

233
00:14:24,563 --> 00:14:26,065
Hold on here!

234
00:14:26,131 --> 00:14:27,132
Dr. Kaji?

235
00:14:27,366 --> 00:14:31,971
Hara, from now on,
refer to me as Director Kaji.

236
00:14:32,404 --> 00:14:34,039
I'm Dr. Kaji. It's nice to meet you.

237
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:35,374
This is nuts!

238
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:36,642
What's with this "intelligent?"

239
00:14:36,742 --> 00:14:38,911
"Genome?" And that "minimally invasive?"

240
00:14:38,978 --> 00:14:40,112
When were those names made up?

241
00:14:40,179 --> 00:14:42,081
You may act big now,

242
00:14:42,181 --> 00:14:44,650
but you cold-blooded cost cutter,

243
00:14:44,750 --> 00:14:47,052
you'll be fired in no time,
just like that!

244
00:14:47,319 --> 00:14:50,055
- You call this streamlining?
- This is unacceptable!

245
00:14:50,456 --> 00:14:51,991
Kaji, I'm taking over!

246
00:14:52,057 --> 00:14:53,893
If we lose our jobs,
there will be trouble!

247
00:14:53,959 --> 00:14:54,827
Stop it, Dr. Ebina!

248
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:56,729
- Calm down! You too, Dr. Kaji!
- Cut it out!

249
00:15:04,169 --> 00:15:05,604
Who's that woman?

250
00:15:05,704 --> 00:15:06,739
Dr. Daimon.

251
00:15:07,206 --> 00:15:10,209
- Demon? What is she doing here?
- Long time no see, Daimon!

252
00:15:10,376 --> 00:15:11,543
I'm on the verge of being fired.

253
00:15:11,610 --> 00:15:12,745
You're frightening.

254
00:15:13,279 --> 00:15:14,680
TOTEI

255
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:16,148
I'm Michiko Daimon.

256
00:15:16,548 --> 00:15:18,017
It's been a while, everyone.

257
00:15:20,519 --> 00:15:23,289
Dr. Michiko Daimon.

258
00:15:24,390 --> 00:15:28,694
What are you doing
at Totei University Hospital?

259
00:15:29,028 --> 00:15:31,530
Isn't it obvious? To perform surgery.

260
00:15:33,999 --> 00:15:36,101
Don't be stupid.

261
00:15:37,603 --> 00:15:39,905
Totei University Hospital is

262
00:15:39,972 --> 00:15:44,310
in the middle of executing
painful reforms.

263
00:15:45,144 --> 00:15:47,046
There's no way

264
00:15:47,413 --> 00:15:52,451
we'll hire a freelance surgeon
with high fees like you.

265
00:15:59,191 --> 00:16:02,328
As usual, thank you for
the sight of your pretty legs.

266
00:16:02,428 --> 00:16:04,063
Therefore,

267
00:16:04,129 --> 00:16:07,566
our hospital has no use for you.

268
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:09,268
Please leave.

269
00:16:10,936 --> 00:16:13,939
It's been a while,
Hospital Director Hiruma.

270
00:16:14,006 --> 00:16:15,407
Yes, it has.

271
00:16:15,641 --> 00:16:21,146
We're here now at the request of
Assistant Director Nicholas Tange.

272
00:16:22,081 --> 00:16:23,082
Really?

273
00:16:24,149 --> 00:16:26,685
Yes, they are, as is Dr. Daimon here.

274
00:16:26,785 --> 00:16:27,786
What?

275
00:16:27,853 --> 00:16:30,589
Why are you hiring this hack doctor?
It makes no sense!

276
00:16:30,823 --> 00:16:32,925
Why don't you ask Nichotan?

277
00:16:33,025 --> 00:16:34,159
"Nichotan"?

278
00:16:34,460 --> 00:16:36,028
Where is Nichotan?

279
00:16:36,095 --> 00:16:38,564
- Who the heck is "Nichotan"?
- Where is he?

280
00:16:40,499 --> 00:16:41,834
Assistant Director Tange is...

281
00:16:54,013 --> 00:16:55,014
<i>Ole!</i>

282
00:16:57,149 --> 00:17:00,386
There you go. Eat up!

283
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,655
Well then, let's dig in.

284
00:17:04,056 --> 00:17:05,524
Thank you!

285
00:17:06,492 --> 00:17:09,461
Thanks to your hard work,

286
00:17:09,762 --> 00:17:12,331
the doctors can do their best
and the patients are healthy.

287
00:17:12,398 --> 00:17:15,300
You're the angels
that support this hospital.

288
00:17:16,568 --> 00:17:19,905
He called us angels!

289
00:17:21,173 --> 00:17:22,374
That's hot.

290
00:17:25,010 --> 00:17:26,879
- That's good.
- Delicious!

291
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:31,884
We finally have someone
who understands us.

292
00:17:31,984 --> 00:17:36,922
He may not look like it, but he is
the new assistant hospital director.

293
00:17:37,689 --> 00:17:39,792
This is Nicholas Tange?

294
00:17:40,292 --> 00:17:41,860
You're that guy?

295
00:17:41,927 --> 00:17:43,429
You know him?

296
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:50,369
Welcome, Dr. Daimon.

297
00:17:50,536 --> 00:17:52,604
It's good to see you again, Nichotan.

298
00:17:52,838 --> 00:17:56,542
It's a pleasure to be working with you,
Dr. Michiko Daimon.

299
00:17:56,608 --> 00:17:58,043
One moment, please.

300
00:17:58,477 --> 00:18:00,879
Just to be sure,
before signing the contract,

301
00:18:00,979 --> 00:18:04,983
I would like to review
Michiko Daimon's contract conditions.

302
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:09,588
Here you are.

303
00:18:12,091 --> 00:18:14,493
Here. Please pass these around.

304
00:18:17,563 --> 00:18:18,397
CONTRACT

305
00:18:18,464 --> 00:18:19,865
They're doing this again?

306
00:18:19,932 --> 00:18:21,867
It's my sixth time. I don't need it.

307
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:23,902
- I don't either.
- What the heck is this?

308
00:18:24,503 --> 00:18:28,107
- "For example, research for papers."
- I decline.

309
00:18:28,173 --> 00:18:30,142
- "Attending medical conferences."
- I decline.

310
00:18:30,209 --> 00:18:32,244
- "Giving rides to golf."
- I decline.

311
00:18:32,344 --> 00:18:34,780
- "Covering up for meetings with lovers."
- I decline.

312
00:18:35,214 --> 00:18:36,248
Et cetera.

313
00:18:36,782 --> 00:18:40,586
I will not do anything
I don't need a doctor's license for.

314
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:42,588
That is all.

315
00:18:45,090 --> 00:18:46,258
That is not all.

316
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:47,926
Who do you think you are?

317
00:18:48,026 --> 00:18:48,961
Dr. Daimon,

318
00:18:50,162 --> 00:18:52,965
you are my ideal surgeon.

319
00:18:56,001 --> 00:18:57,136
I welcome you,

320
00:18:57,302 --> 00:18:58,937
my friend in reforms!

321
00:19:00,772 --> 00:19:02,641
Oh, how nice!

322
00:19:02,708 --> 00:19:04,576
I wish he would do that to me too!

323
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:08,247
I look forward to this.

324
00:19:09,481 --> 00:19:10,449
"I look forward to this?"

325
00:19:10,516 --> 00:19:12,217
Instead of "I decline,"
she looks forward to it!

326
00:19:12,584 --> 00:19:15,053
- I look forward to this too.
- Good.

327
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:25,097
<i>Oh, how nice!
I wish he would do that to me too!</i>

328
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:27,666
The assistant director sure is popular.

329
00:19:28,133 --> 00:19:31,670
Michiko Daimon is smiling.

330
00:19:32,604 --> 00:19:34,740
I can't believe this. What's going on?

331
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,241
I couldn't believe my eyes.

332
00:19:36,808 --> 00:19:38,143
It's unbelievable.

333
00:19:39,111 --> 00:19:40,279
I can't believe this.

334
00:19:42,047 --> 00:19:43,815
How could my satellite hospital be closed?

335
00:19:43,882 --> 00:19:45,150
Why did you come in here?

336
00:19:45,384 --> 00:19:47,853
Hospital Director, is there some way
you could accept this?

337
00:19:50,389 --> 00:19:52,658
- Have mercy upon me.
- What is this?

338
00:19:53,458 --> 00:19:55,460
Oh, <i>marimo</i> sweet buns.
Souvenirs from Hokkaido.

339
00:19:56,695 --> 00:19:58,764
Wow, they look delicious.

340
00:19:59,665 --> 00:20:01,967
Want one? Have one if you like.

341
00:20:02,334 --> 00:20:05,537
Well, actually... That's not it.

342
00:20:06,104 --> 00:20:07,172
This here...

343
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:15,147
- Ebina.
- Yes?

344
00:20:15,547 --> 00:20:17,616
- Cut this stuff out.
- But

345
00:20:17,683 --> 00:20:20,419
at this rate, even though I've got
a medical license,

346
00:20:20,652 --> 00:20:24,256
my life as a doctor will...
Wait, I have one more.

347
00:20:25,857 --> 00:20:27,559
My life as a doctor will be over.

348
00:20:27,759 --> 00:20:29,294
I told you to cut it out!

349
00:20:30,295 --> 00:20:33,498
Why don't you try being a taxi driver?

350
00:20:33,832 --> 00:20:36,768
You need an advanced
class-2 license to be a taxi driver.

351
00:20:36,868 --> 00:20:38,303
I could never get that.

352
00:20:38,370 --> 00:20:41,473
Why don't you try to pass the test?

353
00:20:41,540 --> 00:20:44,109
- Tests are even worse.
- What?

354
00:20:44,409 --> 00:20:47,045
Now that it has come to this,
I'll be perfectly honest.

355
00:20:47,512 --> 00:20:49,881
Before getting into Totei University,

356
00:20:50,015 --> 00:20:52,284
I only got into
Saint Michael Medical University

357
00:20:52,384 --> 00:20:55,053
because my dad sold all his fields
and paid for me to get in.

358
00:20:55,153 --> 00:20:56,655
You bribed your way in?

359
00:20:57,723 --> 00:20:58,557
Yes.

360
00:20:59,024 --> 00:21:03,061
Then go out the back door too.

361
00:21:04,162 --> 00:21:05,764
- You're so mean.
- Dr. Ebina...

362
00:21:05,864 --> 00:21:07,532
- Quit crying!
- Director...

363
00:21:08,900 --> 00:21:10,402
Oh, fine. Wait!

364
00:21:11,903 --> 00:21:13,105
You'll hire me?

365
00:21:13,171 --> 00:21:14,706
Don't be stupid!

366
00:21:15,240 --> 00:21:18,243
Well, I'll let you in as a plebe.

367
00:21:18,644 --> 00:21:23,849
If you don't mind being a plebe,
I'll hire you at this hospital.

368
00:21:24,516 --> 00:21:27,386
Plebe? You mean at the bottom?

369
00:21:27,452 --> 00:21:28,420
At the bottom.

370
00:21:30,722 --> 00:21:32,624
HOT SPRING

371
00:21:32,691 --> 00:21:34,493
<i>I'm broke!</i>

372
00:21:35,627 --> 00:21:39,531
We were kicked out of my agency
by my last landlord.

373
00:21:40,098 --> 00:21:43,602
Moving expenses and other stuff are
making it hard for me too.

374
00:21:43,702 --> 00:21:45,904
Isn't that right, Ben Casey?

375
00:21:46,605 --> 00:21:48,040
Earn your keep.

376
00:21:48,707 --> 00:21:53,011
No wonder you didn't say "I decline"
when the assistant director hugged you.

377
00:21:53,378 --> 00:21:56,214
You've mellowed, haven't you, Ms. Daimon?

378
00:21:56,381 --> 00:21:58,884
Nichotan is pretty cool for an old guy.

379
00:21:58,950 --> 00:22:00,585
He's a good cook. He's hip.

380
00:22:00,652 --> 00:22:03,922
What's more, he lives in that house
in the middle of the forest.

381
00:22:04,022 --> 00:22:06,858
You mean everyone living in a house
in the middle of nowhere is good?

382
00:22:06,925 --> 00:22:07,826
Yes.

383
00:22:08,694 --> 00:22:13,065
Nicholas Tange, a second-generation
Japanese-Brazilian.

384
00:22:13,265 --> 00:22:16,268
When his father's coffee farm went
bankrupt as a child,

385
00:22:16,335 --> 00:22:17,469
his family was ruined.

386
00:22:18,537 --> 00:22:19,571
Useless.

387
00:22:22,774 --> 00:22:23,775
This is useless too.

388
00:22:24,409 --> 00:22:28,246
<i>Young Nicholas graduated
from Sao Paulo Medical University</i>

389
00:22:28,347 --> 00:22:32,217
<i>on student loans and while working
as a dishwasher and cook.</i>

390
00:22:32,384 --> 00:22:34,986
<i>He also obtained
a Japanese medical license.</i>

391
00:22:35,053 --> 00:22:39,424
<i>Then, as an investor, he has saved
numerous failing companies</i>

392
00:22:39,524 --> 00:22:42,327
<i>and climbed the social ladder.</i>

393
00:22:42,427 --> 00:22:43,428
This is useless too.

394
00:22:45,163 --> 00:22:46,732
He's suffered through a lot.

395
00:22:46,865 --> 00:22:50,602
But he's of Latin descent,
so you and he must get along.

396
00:22:51,737 --> 00:22:54,406
At any rate, I've got to make some money!

397
00:22:55,207 --> 00:22:56,308
Akira!

398
00:22:56,408 --> 00:22:57,976
How's my Rat Coin doing?

399
00:22:59,578 --> 00:23:01,413
What the heck is "Rat Coin"?

400
00:23:01,513 --> 00:23:02,748
I'm not really sure,

401
00:23:02,814 --> 00:23:05,517
but it will increase in value
by 100 times if you have it.

402
00:23:05,584 --> 00:23:07,052
- By 100 times?
- That's right.

403
00:23:07,519 --> 00:23:10,155
It feels like my luck is
finally improving.

404
00:23:11,289 --> 00:23:15,861
You know, if we strike it big,
let's move to a beautiful palace.

405
00:23:15,927 --> 00:23:18,697
- Sure thing.
- Michiko, I'm sorry,

406
00:23:18,930 --> 00:23:20,532
but that's a <i>ron</i>!

407
00:23:21,299 --> 00:23:22,701
Big Three Dragons!

408
00:23:24,136 --> 00:23:28,140
You can get it all back easily
when it increases 100 times.

409
00:23:28,974 --> 00:23:30,709
You're right!

410
00:23:30,942 --> 00:23:35,046
You're so right! Let's play again.

411
00:23:35,947 --> 00:23:40,652
<i>Hospital Director Hiruma will now
make a round of visits.</i>

412
00:23:42,421 --> 00:23:44,289
The assistant hospital director
has arrived.

413
00:23:46,458 --> 00:23:49,060
Good morning, Assistant Director.

414
00:23:49,828 --> 00:23:51,096
- Hospital Director Hiruma.
- Yes?

415
00:23:51,563 --> 00:23:53,732
- What is this?
- This?

416
00:23:54,166 --> 00:24:00,005
You could call this an important
ceremony in which us doctors

417
00:24:00,238 --> 00:24:03,575
strengthen our ties with the patients.

418
00:24:03,942 --> 00:24:04,976
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

419
00:24:10,282 --> 00:24:12,451
Dr. Daimon.

420
00:24:12,951 --> 00:24:18,190
The least you can do is arrive
before the director's rounds.

421
00:24:18,423 --> 00:24:20,559
I'm in time for surgery.
Is there a problem?

422
00:24:20,792 --> 00:24:23,361
Dr. Daimon,
focus only on performing surgeries.

423
00:24:23,562 --> 00:24:25,664
You don't have to do anything else.

424
00:24:26,131 --> 00:24:28,567
Nichotan, you're the best.

425
00:24:36,107 --> 00:24:37,742
- Did she just wink?
- That's scary.

426
00:24:40,245 --> 00:24:43,014
That smile of hers was so cute!

427
00:24:43,081 --> 00:24:45,617
I've never seen Daimon
look so sweet before.

428
00:24:46,785 --> 00:24:48,386
You're here, Dr. Ebina?

429
00:24:48,453 --> 00:24:50,922
Yes, I've been here the whole time.
I'll be here from now on.

430
00:24:51,490 --> 00:24:56,027
I'm Takashi Ebina.
I'll be your colleague from now on.

431
00:24:56,161 --> 00:24:57,128
What?

432
00:24:57,229 --> 00:24:59,164
You know, for the sake of surviving,

433
00:24:59,531 --> 00:25:01,566
you need change and challenge.

434
00:25:01,733 --> 00:25:02,901
- Nice to work with you.
- Oh, yes.

435
00:25:02,968 --> 00:25:04,603
Director's rounds!

436
00:25:07,239 --> 00:25:09,307
- Where's your "yes, sir?"
- Yes, sir!

437
00:25:11,543 --> 00:25:13,211
This is all useless.

438
00:25:13,845 --> 00:25:15,480
Yes, sir.

439
00:25:16,681 --> 00:25:18,083
DIRECTOR'S ROUNDS

440
00:25:18,984 --> 00:25:20,519
ELIMINATE

441
00:25:21,386 --> 00:25:25,290
Let us see Nicholas Tange show his skill.

442
00:25:26,691 --> 00:25:31,062
This place will soon be in the middle of
a cost-cutting storm.

443
00:25:34,366 --> 00:25:37,369
<i>Reduce the average consultation
from eight minutes to five.</i>

444
00:25:37,769 --> 00:25:40,105
<i>Eighty percent of outpatient visits
must be by reservation.</i>

445
00:25:40,338 --> 00:25:43,308
<i>Drastically cut outpatient visit.</i>

446
00:25:43,475 --> 00:25:45,744
<i>Increase consultation efficiency
by 40 percent.</i>

447
00:25:45,944 --> 00:25:47,946
<i>Increase revenue by ten percent.</i>

448
00:25:48,480 --> 00:25:51,983
<i>If bed occupancy increases by
twenty-five percent,</i>

449
00:25:52,417 --> 00:25:54,219
<i>revenue will increase by eight percent.</i>

450
00:25:54,419 --> 00:25:57,289
This four-patient room
can hold six patients.

451
00:25:57,822 --> 00:26:00,525
We can handle ten more
gastrointestinal inpatients

452
00:26:00,625 --> 00:26:01,626
from this afternoon.

453
00:26:02,494 --> 00:26:03,762
BED OCCUPANCY

454
00:26:04,229 --> 00:26:08,133
<i>The current revenue per doctor
at Totei University Hospital is</i>

455
00:26:08,466 --> 00:26:10,368
<i>a mere 35 million.</i>

456
00:26:10,835 --> 00:26:13,204
<i>To make it profitable,</i>

457
00:26:13,371 --> 00:26:15,740
<i>it must be raised to at least 100 million.</i>

458
00:26:18,043 --> 00:26:19,110
Complete.

459
00:26:19,177 --> 00:26:20,545
- Good work.
- Good work.

460
00:26:20,946 --> 00:26:22,814
Let's all go for lunch today.

461
00:26:22,881 --> 00:26:24,950
Great! Thank you.

462
00:26:25,383 --> 00:26:28,620
<i>The biggest problem is
the limited number of surgeries.</i>

463
00:26:29,654 --> 00:26:31,456
When is the next surgery?

464
00:26:31,923 --> 00:26:33,024
Oh, Assistant Director.

465
00:26:33,325 --> 00:26:34,559
In four hours.

466
00:26:35,260 --> 00:26:36,928
<i>Four empty hours is a waste.</i>

467
00:26:37,028 --> 00:26:39,631
You can do a stomach cancer surgery
in that time.

468
00:26:40,098 --> 00:26:41,666
I'll adjust the surgeons' shift.

469
00:26:42,400 --> 00:26:45,070
- We'll have lunch another time.
- Right.

470
00:26:52,577 --> 00:26:55,146
She's fast. Magnificent.

471
00:26:55,213 --> 00:26:57,682
Hemorrhaging stopped.
I'm closing. 3-0 suture.

472
00:26:57,949 --> 00:26:58,984
- Quickly.
- Right.

473
00:26:59,284 --> 00:27:02,287
<i>Can I give you a total stomach excision
in an hour?</i>

474
00:27:02,387 --> 00:27:04,990
I'll finish this in ten minutes.
I don't need an hour.

475
00:27:05,156 --> 00:27:06,224
What about a break?

476
00:27:06,658 --> 00:27:09,561
<i>My specialty is surgery
and my hobby is surgery.</i>

477
00:27:10,962 --> 00:27:12,731
Incredible.

478
00:27:12,831 --> 00:27:14,899
Room 1, you're being too aggressive.

479
00:27:15,266 --> 00:27:16,768
Add another centimeter of margin.

480
00:27:18,737 --> 00:27:20,905
<i>Okay. Will do.</i>

481
00:27:21,139 --> 00:27:23,241
Room 4, you're slowing down.

482
00:27:23,575 --> 00:27:25,110
Operate more efficiently.

483
00:27:28,480 --> 00:27:31,449
I'm starving after four surgeries.

484
00:27:35,153 --> 00:27:36,721
Thank you for this food.

485
00:27:37,322 --> 00:27:43,428
Is that right? How can they scold
such a hard worker like you?

486
00:27:43,528 --> 00:27:46,564
The world really has gone crazy.

487
00:27:46,831 --> 00:27:48,700
I need the money.

488
00:27:48,933 --> 00:27:53,571
My little brothers are still young.
I need to send money home.

489
00:27:54,139 --> 00:27:55,473
You're so kind.

490
00:27:56,207 --> 00:27:59,844
I'm unbelievably healthy,

491
00:27:59,978 --> 00:28:02,547
so I've worked until this ripe old age.

492
00:28:03,348 --> 00:28:06,551
"Stay hungry, stay foolish."

493
00:28:06,751 --> 00:28:09,220
Those are the words of Mr. Jobs,
whom I respect.

494
00:28:09,287 --> 00:28:11,289
That was impressive.

495
00:28:11,656 --> 00:28:15,527
It's very supportive of good old honest,
hardworking Japanese

496
00:28:15,660 --> 00:28:18,430
like you two are.

497
00:28:18,963 --> 00:28:22,867
Oh, dear me! "Impressive"? You exaggerate!

498
00:28:25,603 --> 00:28:26,705
What's the matter?

499
00:28:27,972 --> 00:28:29,007
Madam Iwata?

500
00:28:29,908 --> 00:28:31,176
- Give me this.
- Sure.

501
00:28:35,814 --> 00:28:39,284
I just got a little dizzy. I'm fine.

502
00:28:39,517 --> 00:28:41,619
Let's get you a heart and chest exam.

503
00:28:41,986 --> 00:28:44,322
I told you, I'm just fine.

504
00:28:44,422 --> 00:28:45,590
Let's go.

505
00:28:45,657 --> 00:28:47,025
Dr. Daimon is a great doctor.

506
00:28:47,459 --> 00:28:49,494
You should do as she tells you.

507
00:28:50,428 --> 00:28:53,164
If you say so, Assistant Director,
then I will.

508
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:03,241
He's completely different from
the previous hospital directors.

509
00:29:03,475 --> 00:29:06,544
Mr. Tange is so kind to people like us,

510
00:29:06,711 --> 00:29:09,214
and he's handsome too.

511
00:29:09,280 --> 00:29:10,782
I wonder if he's single!

512
00:29:11,049 --> 00:29:12,884
That hurts!

513
00:29:13,184 --> 00:29:15,053
I told you. Don't move.

514
00:29:21,159 --> 00:29:26,231
<i>There's a possibility of pulmonary
embolism and deep vein thrombosis.</i>

515
00:29:26,297 --> 00:29:27,365
Who was that?

516
00:29:27,465 --> 00:29:29,367
The AI diagnosis device
the assistant director adopted.

517
00:29:29,868 --> 00:29:32,971
<i>It's nice to meet you. I'm the AI, Ai.</i>

518
00:29:33,505 --> 00:29:38,376
<i>I use artificial intelligence to
diagnose you quickly and accurately.</i>

519
00:29:39,410 --> 00:29:43,014
So is a pulmonary embolism
a serious illness?

520
00:29:43,081 --> 00:29:44,215
Your blood pressure is low,

521
00:29:44,282 --> 00:29:46,851
so let's get you on
an IV and hospitalize you.

522
00:29:46,951 --> 00:29:48,520
We'll give you more tests tomorrow.

523
00:29:48,720 --> 00:29:50,889
There's no way I'm getting hospitalized!

524
00:29:51,089 --> 00:29:52,791
I have to get back to work.

525
00:29:52,857 --> 00:29:55,059
You'll die if you don't do as I tell you.

526
00:29:56,094 --> 00:29:57,162
What?

527
00:29:57,262 --> 00:29:59,164
<i>That was an inappropriate remark.</i>

528
00:29:59,497 --> 00:30:01,966
- Shut your trap, Ai!
- Cut that out, Dr. Daimon!

529
00:30:02,066 --> 00:30:04,302
- This cost hundreds of millions!
- It's annoying!

530
00:30:04,369 --> 00:30:05,537
It is not annoying.

531
00:30:05,737 --> 00:30:07,238
<i>In order to revitalize</i>

532
00:30:07,372 --> 00:30:10,642
<i>this inefficient, unproductive
Totei University Hospital,</i>

533
00:30:10,742 --> 00:30:14,479
<i>I have employed an AI system
for the entire hospital.</i>

534
00:30:18,082 --> 00:30:19,350
<i>- Let's begin.
- Let's begin.</i>

535
00:30:19,417 --> 00:30:21,052
An AI-assisted surgery is about to begin.

536
00:30:26,257 --> 00:30:28,960
<i>- It will be over soon.
- I'm counting on you.</i>

537
00:30:39,370 --> 00:30:40,271
It's Madam Iwata!

538
00:30:48,947 --> 00:30:51,516
What's going on here? She's my patient.

539
00:30:53,084 --> 00:30:57,188
The AI diagnosed this patient
with a pulmonary embolism.

540
00:30:57,255 --> 00:30:59,057
We still haven't done
a contrast-enhanced CT scan.

541
00:30:59,157 --> 00:31:00,925
We're not certain
it's a pulmonary embolism!

542
00:31:02,927 --> 00:31:04,028
Daimon!

543
00:31:04,729 --> 00:31:08,600
<i>I'm calculating. Preparing for surgery.</i>

544
00:31:08,700 --> 00:31:11,202
- Stop! You can't go in there!
- Madam Iwata!

545
00:31:11,502 --> 00:31:13,204
Dr. Daimon, what are you doing here?

546
00:31:13,671 --> 00:31:15,907
Mr. Tange says that if I get surgery

547
00:31:15,974 --> 00:31:19,811
to clear my clogged arteries,
I'll live a long life.

548
00:31:20,144 --> 00:31:21,813
I really appreciate this.

549
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:24,549
Listen, let's not have this surgery today.

550
00:31:24,616 --> 00:31:26,584
- What?
- What are you talking about?

551
00:31:26,684 --> 00:31:28,786
Dr. Daimon is worried.

552
00:31:28,920 --> 00:31:31,723
She's worried that Madam Iwata is
afraid of being operated on.

553
00:31:32,223 --> 00:31:35,326
I'm not such a coward.

554
00:31:36,361 --> 00:31:39,364
Let's get more tests done.
You'll be fine if we do it now.

555
00:31:39,464 --> 00:31:42,867
Quit bothering us.
Kick this lady doctor out.

556
00:31:42,934 --> 00:31:44,869
- Okay.
- Madam Iwata, my idea is much better.

557
00:31:44,936 --> 00:31:47,472
- Don't make us repeat it!
- Get out, Dr. Daimon!

558
00:31:47,739 --> 00:31:49,641
Madam Iwata!

559
00:31:52,377 --> 00:31:55,680
I think that guy's
nothing more than a con man.

560
00:31:56,247 --> 00:31:58,216
- Who are you talking about?
- Nichotan.

561
00:31:58,816 --> 00:32:01,152
Then he's a heck of a con man.

562
00:32:01,219 --> 00:32:02,453
You know what?

563
00:32:02,520 --> 00:32:06,691
If cost cutters aren't
great communicators, they don't succeed.

564
00:32:07,091 --> 00:32:08,893
It says so in that book.

565
00:32:11,129 --> 00:32:12,530
What a load of garbage.

566
00:32:13,164 --> 00:32:17,769
Forget about that.
Rat Coin is going up again.

567
00:32:21,739 --> 00:32:23,508
It's doing fantastic!

568
00:32:27,745 --> 00:32:30,548
What? You're already working?

569
00:32:30,615 --> 00:32:32,083
Are you sure you're okay?

570
00:32:32,183 --> 00:32:34,919
I owe my life to
the assistant hospital director.

571
00:32:35,019 --> 00:32:36,287
Thanks to him, I feel great!

572
00:32:37,822 --> 00:32:39,324
That hurts...

573
00:32:39,891 --> 00:32:41,092
Are you all right?

574
00:32:41,492 --> 00:32:44,362
- I'm sorry.
- Please be careful.

575
00:32:44,862 --> 00:32:47,832
Madam Iwata,
your right arm hurts, doesn't it?

576
00:32:48,399 --> 00:32:50,101
Let's test you again. Come on.

577
00:32:50,201 --> 00:32:53,371
What? Are you going to scare me
by telling me I'll die again?

578
00:32:53,471 --> 00:32:54,739
Just come!

579
00:32:56,307 --> 00:32:57,308
Here you are.

580
00:32:57,642 --> 00:32:58,910
Assistant Hospital Director!

581
00:32:59,644 --> 00:33:02,046
- Please help me.
- What's the matter?

582
00:33:02,747 --> 00:33:06,250
Thanks to the surgery, I'm working again.

583
00:33:06,351 --> 00:33:07,752
Thank you.

584
00:33:07,819 --> 00:33:12,090
But even so, she's scaring me again.

585
00:33:12,190 --> 00:33:14,292
She says I'll die if I don't get tests.

586
00:33:15,293 --> 00:33:16,661
Dr. Daimon,

587
00:33:17,261 --> 00:33:21,099
please refrain from conduct that
causes a post-op patient to worry.

588
00:33:21,165 --> 00:33:24,669
Listen. Was that operation
really necessary?

589
00:33:25,670 --> 00:33:26,771
What do you mean by that?

590
00:33:30,174 --> 00:33:32,143
Please stop doing this
in front of a patient.

591
00:33:32,610 --> 00:33:34,278
There's no need to worry.

592
00:33:34,479 --> 00:33:36,014
The surgery was a success.

593
00:33:36,147 --> 00:33:38,783
Today, I came to celebrate your recovery.

594
00:33:44,522 --> 00:33:47,392
Go ahead. These were made by
Assistant Hospital Director Tange.

595
00:33:47,458 --> 00:33:49,360
Oh, my! <i>Inari</i> sushi!

596
00:33:50,028 --> 00:33:52,630
These are so delicious.

597
00:33:52,830 --> 00:33:54,966
Come, everyone. Help yourselves.

598
00:33:55,533 --> 00:33:58,136
- Hey, you guys.
- Help yourself, Dr. Daimon.

599
00:33:58,202 --> 00:34:00,505
- Let's have some.
- Those look good.

600
00:34:00,738 --> 00:34:03,708
Can I have one too? Thank you.

601
00:34:07,845 --> 00:34:09,180
Oh, dear!

602
00:34:10,181 --> 00:34:11,215
Are you okay?

603
00:34:14,085 --> 00:34:15,420
Oxygen, now!

604
00:34:15,520 --> 00:34:18,256
Contact the lab and radiology!
Get a stretcher now!

605
00:34:22,460 --> 00:34:25,897
Five days ago, Ichiko Iwata, age 64,
a food service staff member here,

606
00:34:25,963 --> 00:34:29,200
underwent a catheter-directed
thrombolysis for pulmonary embolism.

607
00:34:29,367 --> 00:34:32,336
Today, she suffered
respiratory distress and hemoptysis.

608
00:34:32,537 --> 00:34:33,971
A two-centimeter tumor

609
00:34:34,072 --> 00:34:36,641
suspected of causing
pleural effusion in right lung S1.

610
00:34:36,974 --> 00:34:39,343
In other words, Pancoast lung cancer.

611
00:34:41,012 --> 00:34:42,980
That's why I said she needed
a contrast-enhanced CT scan.

612
00:34:45,283 --> 00:34:46,384
Seriously?

613
00:34:46,451 --> 00:34:48,853
Does this mean the AI misdiagnosed her?

614
00:34:50,188 --> 00:34:51,522
What is AI Ai's diagnosis?

615
00:34:52,023 --> 00:34:54,492
She believes operative treatment
is impossible.

616
00:34:55,226 --> 00:34:58,529
It's time for the Oncology Department
to take over.

617
00:34:58,629 --> 00:35:01,999
We'll conduct chemotherapy
and radiation therapy.

618
00:35:02,366 --> 00:35:06,370
We'll simultaneously administer
carboplatin and paclitaxel.

619
00:35:06,838 --> 00:35:07,839
Yes, ma'am.

620
00:35:07,905 --> 00:35:11,309
But the five-year rate of survival
for that treatment is twenty percent.

621
00:35:11,375 --> 00:35:12,477
That's what the AI says.

622
00:35:12,543 --> 00:35:13,778
That's all it helps?

623
00:35:13,845 --> 00:35:17,615
The patient is advanced in age.
No treatment is perfect.

624
00:35:17,682 --> 00:35:18,649
I'll operate on her.

625
00:35:19,083 --> 00:35:21,252
You just want to operate, right?

626
00:35:21,352 --> 00:35:24,489
- You stay out of this!
- She was originally my patient.

627
00:35:24,589 --> 00:35:26,891
Compared to medication,
the chance of survival

628
00:35:26,991 --> 00:35:29,560
after surgery is ten percent lower, right?

629
00:35:30,561 --> 00:35:33,097
Yes, according to the AI's analysis.

630
00:35:33,164 --> 00:35:36,701
You sound like a fool
who can only obey the AI.

631
00:35:37,001 --> 00:35:39,871
So...

632
00:35:41,539 --> 00:35:43,541
- Who's that again?
- Intelligent.

633
00:35:43,608 --> 00:35:46,978
I'm Director Ushio of
Next-Generation Intelligent Surgery.

634
00:35:47,044 --> 00:35:48,179
That's long.

635
00:35:48,613 --> 00:35:50,381
I didn't make up the name.

636
00:35:50,481 --> 00:35:51,649
I don't care about that.

637
00:35:51,749 --> 00:35:52,950
You're the one who asked.

638
00:35:53,017 --> 00:35:55,286
The surgery the AI directed
was a failure, right?

639
00:35:55,386 --> 00:35:56,621
It was not a failure.

640
00:35:57,488 --> 00:35:59,490
The clotting was completely cleared.

641
00:35:59,590 --> 00:36:01,526
But you missed the tumor.

642
00:36:01,826 --> 00:36:04,729
At that time, she hadn't complained
of right-arm pain.

643
00:36:05,129 --> 00:36:08,366
The tumor was hidden from
the x-ray by her clavicle.

644
00:36:08,766 --> 00:36:10,701
The AI simply didn't see it.

645
00:36:10,968 --> 00:36:12,370
Oh, man.

646
00:36:13,771 --> 00:36:16,741
How dare a doctor blame
their own mistake on the patient.

647
00:36:17,975 --> 00:36:21,646
That's why you need to leave this
to internal medicine.

648
00:36:21,746 --> 00:36:24,215
So...

649
00:36:25,583 --> 00:36:26,651
Genome.

650
00:36:26,751 --> 00:36:29,854
I'm Director Hamachi of
Next-Generation Genome Oncology.

651
00:36:30,054 --> 00:36:33,824
And don't you blame the patient
when you can't save them.

652
00:36:35,159 --> 00:36:38,763
At any rate, as for the woman
who this man nearly killed,

653
00:36:38,863 --> 00:36:40,898
I will operate on her and save her.

654
00:36:45,770 --> 00:36:47,371
The assistant hospital director
was listening!

655
00:36:50,174 --> 00:36:51,742
If you are that insistent,

656
00:36:52,476 --> 00:36:55,580
then I would like you to
operate on her again, Dr. Daimon.

657
00:36:56,247 --> 00:36:58,182
Don't underestimate Daimon.

658
00:36:58,616 --> 00:37:02,153
She'll do whatever it takes
to perform surgeries.

659
00:37:02,420 --> 00:37:04,422
You must agree to one condition though.

660
00:37:05,489 --> 00:37:07,725
The AI's diagnosis was not wrong.

661
00:37:08,092 --> 00:37:11,762
If you operate under
the instructions of the AI,

662
00:37:12,463 --> 00:37:15,566
then you may proceed, Dr. Daimon.

663
00:37:22,473 --> 00:37:23,975
What will you do, Daimon?

664
00:37:24,942 --> 00:37:25,977
Are you out?

665
00:37:27,812 --> 00:37:29,280
Of course, I'm not out.

666
00:37:34,852 --> 00:37:35,953
Nichotan.

667
00:37:44,562 --> 00:37:47,565
You know, that Nichotan is
a real cheapskate.

668
00:37:47,898 --> 00:37:50,067
He has really cut wages for operations.

669
00:37:50,268 --> 00:37:51,202
Seriously?

670
00:37:51,936 --> 00:37:56,173
But I came because I wanted to work
with you, Daimon. It's been a while.

671
00:38:01,746 --> 00:38:04,515
I've seen her at another hospital.

672
00:38:04,582 --> 00:38:05,950
She secretly works the night shift.

673
00:38:08,019 --> 00:38:09,920
- She will be fired if you tell.
- What?

674
00:38:10,221 --> 00:38:11,989
I would never tell our hospital.

675
00:38:25,002 --> 00:38:26,570
We will now perform--

676
00:38:26,637 --> 00:38:30,107
<i>We will now perform a combined
right superior pulmonary lobe</i>

677
00:38:30,174 --> 00:38:32,410
<i>and thoracic wall resection
on Ichiko Iwata.</i>

678
00:38:34,645 --> 00:38:38,316
- Vitals--
- <i>BP, 123 over 76.</i>

679
00:38:38,382 --> 00:38:41,319
<i>Pulse, 65, sinus.</i>

680
00:38:42,920 --> 00:38:44,188
Did you get that?

681
00:38:46,824 --> 00:38:47,925
Let's do this.

682
00:38:48,926 --> 00:38:50,161
Excuse me.

683
00:38:54,665 --> 00:38:59,770
Now, please begin under the AI's guidance.

684
00:38:59,870 --> 00:39:02,440
- Yes, sir.
- Okay, Nichotan.

685
00:39:02,540 --> 00:39:05,309
<i>Use the scalpel to create
an incision along the right clavicle</i>

686
00:39:05,543 --> 00:39:08,312
<i>and down the center of the sternum.</i>

687
00:39:11,215 --> 00:39:12,316
- Scalpel.
- Here.

688
00:39:20,224 --> 00:39:23,661
Ai is really working hard again today.

689
00:39:23,728 --> 00:39:27,264
Who in the world named the AI "Ai"?

690
00:39:27,898 --> 00:39:29,633
That was me.

691
00:39:30,301 --> 00:39:33,804
Assistant Director Tange
complimented me on my good sense.

692
00:39:34,372 --> 00:39:35,639
What do you think, Ruri?

693
00:39:38,509 --> 00:39:40,244
Oh, I see.

694
00:39:47,017 --> 00:39:48,486
Exposure of sternum complete.

695
00:39:48,552 --> 00:39:51,055
<i>Remove right sternoclavicular joint.</i>

696
00:39:52,022 --> 00:39:53,224
- Cooper scissors.
- Here.

697
00:40:05,636 --> 00:40:07,471
Ai, I've removed the joint.

698
00:40:07,938 --> 00:40:10,908
<i>Remove the right first rib.</i>

699
00:40:13,010 --> 00:40:14,145
Rib shears.

700
00:40:20,317 --> 00:40:21,585
She sure is fast.

701
00:40:35,366 --> 00:40:37,268
Combined thoracic wall resection complete.

702
00:40:37,568 --> 00:40:40,171
<i>Insert a chest tube, close the chest,</i>

703
00:40:40,237 --> 00:40:41,405
<i>and complete the surgery.</i>

704
00:40:43,541 --> 00:40:44,775
I decline.

705
00:40:46,410 --> 00:40:48,546
I will also conduct
a right medial lobe resection.

706
00:40:48,612 --> 00:40:49,680
- What?
- Really?

707
00:40:51,215 --> 00:40:53,584
- Central sternum incision. Scalpel.
- Here.

708
00:40:53,651 --> 00:40:55,619
<i>You have deviated from instructions.</i>

709
00:40:55,953 --> 00:40:57,788
<i>Cease this operation.</i>

710
00:40:58,122 --> 00:40:59,657
<i>Cease this operation.</i>

711
00:41:03,327 --> 00:41:05,729
First assistant, get the hooked forceps.

712
00:41:05,830 --> 00:41:07,431
- What?
- Hurry!

713
00:41:10,634 --> 00:41:13,204
Hey, follow the AI's instructions.

714
00:41:16,173 --> 00:41:17,208
Dr. Daimon!

715
00:41:19,844 --> 00:41:21,245
<i>Cease this operation.</i>

716
00:41:22,313 --> 00:41:23,848
<i>Cease this operation.</i>

717
00:41:24,448 --> 00:41:29,820
Do you think she intended to ignore
the AI from the very start?

718
00:41:31,455 --> 00:41:35,860
That's why I told you not to
underestimate Michiko Daimon.

719
00:41:40,898 --> 00:41:43,067
Daimon! Stop!

720
00:41:49,540 --> 00:41:51,575
That's right. Stop.

721
00:41:53,377 --> 00:41:54,445
Get a new nurse in here.

722
00:41:54,545 --> 00:41:57,681
Hey! This is no time for a new nurse!

723
00:41:57,748 --> 00:41:59,049
I told you to quit operating!

724
00:42:00,017 --> 00:42:02,319
You haven't slept, right?
Switch with someone else.

725
00:42:09,326 --> 00:42:13,130
BP has dropped to 70.
Respiration deteriorating severely.

726
00:42:15,900 --> 00:42:17,134
- Gauze!
- Here.

727
00:42:18,302 --> 00:42:19,303
Vasopressor!

728
00:42:21,305 --> 00:42:23,641
- Vasopressor!
- Right!

729
00:42:25,976 --> 00:42:28,145
- Second assistant, suction!
- Right.

730
00:42:28,946 --> 00:42:31,549
<i>Danger!</i>

731
00:42:39,456 --> 00:42:42,726
Dr. Daimon, stop this.

732
00:42:53,938 --> 00:42:55,639
- Narrow-tip Kelly clamp.
- Here.

733
00:43:04,815 --> 00:43:06,016
I'm sorry!

734
00:43:06,083 --> 00:43:07,885
Instead of apologizing, get more.

735
00:43:07,952 --> 00:43:08,786
Right.

736
00:43:11,388 --> 00:43:14,458
BP, 60. Full infusion.

737
00:43:21,665 --> 00:43:24,768
Daimon, if you keep this up,
the patient could die.

738
00:43:25,469 --> 00:43:28,672
Dr. Daimon,
let's stop the hemorrhaging and quit.

739
00:43:29,440 --> 00:43:30,574
We're continuing.

740
00:43:32,209 --> 00:43:33,377
- Gauze.
- Here.

741
00:43:34,778 --> 00:43:36,246
How will you make up for this?

742
00:43:36,347 --> 00:43:37,815
If the patient dies during surgery,

743
00:43:37,881 --> 00:43:39,350
we'll be sued for surgical malpractice!

744
00:43:39,416 --> 00:43:41,051
Who will pay compensation?

745
00:43:41,418 --> 00:43:44,855
This will end my plans for
six simultaneous AI-directed surgeries!

746
00:43:45,255 --> 00:43:47,124
That's two billion dollars down the drain!

747
00:43:48,525 --> 00:43:51,328
Declare it inoperable
and just keep her heart beating!

748
00:43:54,865 --> 00:43:56,667
I'll fire you if you don't obey!

749
00:43:57,468 --> 00:43:58,902
Silence!

750
00:43:59,770 --> 00:44:01,939
Who cares how many billions
of dollars it costs?

751
00:44:04,208 --> 00:44:06,143
I will not let Madam Iwata die!

752
00:44:06,744 --> 00:44:09,179
I never fail.

753
00:44:18,022 --> 00:44:19,123
I'm back.

754
00:44:25,929 --> 00:44:28,465
- Hemorrhage found. Artery clip.
- Here.

755
00:44:52,890 --> 00:44:55,192
I'll continue opening her up.
Metzenbaum scissors.

756
00:44:57,127 --> 00:44:58,362
- Forceps.
- Here.

757
00:45:19,083 --> 00:45:20,217
We're done.

758
00:45:20,317 --> 00:45:24,188
BP, 130 over 84. Pulse, 72, sinus.

759
00:45:24,254 --> 00:45:26,457
Watch out for the chest tube
and her respiration.

760
00:45:28,125 --> 00:45:29,660
That was fantastic, Dr. Daimon.

761
00:45:29,893 --> 00:45:32,062
I haven't seen an operation
as magnificent as that in a while.

762
00:45:39,937 --> 00:45:41,138
Nice work.

763
00:45:44,374 --> 00:45:48,045
It looks like we avoided
a two-billion-dollar loss.

764
00:46:12,803 --> 00:46:17,574
It looks to me
more like the infallible Michiko Daimon

765
00:46:17,708 --> 00:46:22,846
disobeyed the AI and made a mistake.

766
00:46:22,913 --> 00:46:24,848
- Am I wrong?
- This wasn't a mistake.

767
00:46:25,682 --> 00:46:28,852
She noticed damage to the pulmonary artery
in the right medial lobe.

768
00:46:28,952 --> 00:46:32,089
It was part of the process
for the resection.

769
00:46:32,189 --> 00:46:34,525
I believe she became aware of a slight

770
00:46:34,625 --> 00:46:38,162
vascular intima detachment during
the pulmonary embolism surgery.

771
00:46:38,529 --> 00:46:41,431
Besides the nurse dropping
and breaking the glass of medication,

772
00:46:41,498 --> 00:46:44,535
I believe this surgery went entirely
according to Dr. Daimon's plans.

773
00:46:44,635 --> 00:46:46,069
- But the director--
- Forget about that.

774
00:46:46,270 --> 00:46:49,339
That's one heck of a doctor.

775
00:46:49,540 --> 00:46:52,743
It's like Michiko Daimon came back to life
after a terrible disease.

776
00:46:55,445 --> 00:46:56,613
Were you

777
00:46:57,681 --> 00:46:59,650
- in the surgery?
- He wasn't there.

778
00:46:59,750 --> 00:47:01,451
- He wasn't there.
- I wasn't there.

779
00:47:08,826 --> 00:47:10,027
- I'm the director...
- But...

780
00:47:12,129 --> 00:47:14,631
This feels so nice!

781
00:47:14,698 --> 00:47:16,867
You finally got to use it, Michiko.

782
00:47:17,467 --> 00:47:21,371
That's because you got us
a ton in operating fees, right?

783
00:47:22,639 --> 00:47:24,541
This is paradise.

784
00:47:26,677 --> 00:47:31,248
<i>How come the AI failed
during today's surgery?</i>

785
00:47:32,649 --> 00:47:35,586
That wasn't an error by the AI.

786
00:47:36,019 --> 00:47:37,020
Then what was it?

787
00:47:38,222 --> 00:47:41,725
Besides the extremely rare disease
of the patient,

788
00:47:41,825 --> 00:47:43,493
they had an extremely rare complication.

789
00:47:44,361 --> 00:47:47,464
The AI didn't know of enough cases,
so she was uneducated on it.

790
00:47:49,099 --> 00:47:51,001
The AI analyzes the data,

791
00:47:51,368 --> 00:47:54,538
then computes likely scenarios
based on patterns.

792
00:47:54,938 --> 00:47:56,740
It made the most efficient diagnosis.

793
00:47:58,909 --> 00:48:01,745
When you compare
the special cases that it missed,

794
00:48:01,812 --> 00:48:03,881
this case is outside her prediction range.

795
00:48:06,083 --> 00:48:09,887
These two stains way out here are

796
00:48:10,120 --> 00:48:12,923
today's patient's symptoms
and Michiko Daimon's diagnosis.

797
00:48:13,924 --> 00:48:16,693
This means that Michiko Daimon was

798
00:48:16,994 --> 00:48:20,664
able to determine what
this extremely rare case was.

799
00:48:21,431 --> 00:48:25,068
Most likely, she does not
discriminate among patients.

800
00:48:25,535 --> 00:48:26,637
Which means

801
00:48:27,337 --> 00:48:31,942
she's always working with
each patient individually.

802
00:48:33,343 --> 00:48:34,811
To us,

803
00:48:35,445 --> 00:48:38,148
she's an out-of-control employee.

804
00:48:41,652 --> 00:48:43,120
Shall we fire her?

805
00:48:43,620 --> 00:48:44,655
No.

806
00:48:46,223 --> 00:48:48,859
The thing that needs to be
immediately eliminated is...

807
00:49:01,772 --> 00:49:03,707
- What?
- What's going on?

808
00:49:04,808 --> 00:49:06,843
We're from the Tokyo District
Public Prosecutor's Office.

809
00:49:07,411 --> 00:49:09,379
You're Shigekatsu Hiruma, right?

810
00:49:10,347 --> 00:49:12,215
Yes. What's wrong?

811
00:49:13,150 --> 00:49:14,184
Wait!

812
00:49:15,686 --> 00:49:18,488
He's been cleared of
any previous suspicions!

813
00:49:18,588 --> 00:49:19,790
This is a mistake!

814
00:49:19,856 --> 00:49:21,858
If you have to arrest anyone,
let it be me!

815
00:49:21,925 --> 00:49:23,026
What are you talking about?

816
00:49:23,093 --> 00:49:26,296
The director would never give
huge kickbacks to businesses

817
00:49:26,363 --> 00:49:27,764
- for granting contracts!
- Ebina!

818
00:49:27,831 --> 00:49:29,866
He has never sexually harassed
or bullied anyone!

819
00:49:29,933 --> 00:49:31,368
- Ebina!
- Or is it

820
00:49:31,468 --> 00:49:34,137
the bribes to officials
in the Ministry of Education?

821
00:49:34,204 --> 00:49:36,306
- He has never done such a thing!
- Ebina!

822
00:49:36,373 --> 00:49:37,941
Are you involved in this?

823
00:49:39,743 --> 00:49:41,545
No, I know nothing about this.

824
00:49:43,480 --> 00:49:45,182
- Shigekatsu Hiruma.
- Yes?

825
00:49:45,983 --> 00:49:48,251
You're under arrest
for suspected violation of

826
00:49:48,318 --> 00:49:52,222
the Bid Rigging Act in the purchase
of expensive medical equipment.

827
00:49:52,289 --> 00:49:53,190
ARREST WARRANT

828
00:49:53,256 --> 00:49:54,424
Under arrest?

829
00:49:55,292 --> 00:50:01,031
I'm not going to the police station.
I know nothing about this.

830
00:50:01,999 --> 00:50:05,369
You're under arrest,
so you have no choice but to come!

831
00:50:05,435 --> 00:50:07,104
Oh, is that right?

832
00:50:07,771 --> 00:50:09,406
Hold on a second.

833
00:50:09,940 --> 00:50:12,042
I don't think I can walk.
What should I do?

834
00:50:12,376 --> 00:50:14,444
What should I do, Ebina?

835
00:50:14,544 --> 00:50:16,546
- Yes, sir! I'll be right back!
- Okay.

836
00:50:17,881 --> 00:50:19,082
We have this.

837
00:50:22,786 --> 00:50:24,855
- Shall we go?
- Yes, please.

838
00:50:24,921 --> 00:50:25,756
Okay.

839
00:50:32,863 --> 00:50:34,865
I knew it.

840
00:50:37,000 --> 00:50:38,168
I'm the one

841
00:50:38,268 --> 00:50:42,339
who invited you from Brazil
on the other side of the world.

842
00:50:44,374 --> 00:50:50,580
Are you repaying my kindness
with ingratitude?

843
00:50:51,314 --> 00:50:56,119
My job is to save this hospital
which is on the verge of collapse.

844
00:50:57,454 --> 00:50:59,689
To do that, the thing we need least of all

845
00:51:01,858 --> 00:51:03,060
is you.

846
00:51:05,762 --> 00:51:09,132
I'm a familiar face
at the prosecutor's office.

847
00:51:10,267 --> 00:51:13,003
I swear they'll drop the case,
and I'll be back.

848
00:51:14,104 --> 00:51:16,373
I look forward to seeing you then.

849
00:51:18,375 --> 00:51:20,343
- Ebina.
- Yes, sir.

850
00:51:22,679 --> 00:51:23,780
Okay, here we go.

851
00:51:24,815 --> 00:51:26,850
- This is a betrayal by Nicholas.
- Hey.

852
00:51:26,917 --> 00:51:28,218
- Ebina.
- Yes?

853
00:51:28,318 --> 00:51:32,022
Why in the world do you prattle on...

854
00:51:32,089 --> 00:51:36,560
SHIGEKATSU HIRUMA

855
00:51:53,343 --> 00:51:54,644
Excuse me.

856
00:51:57,013 --> 00:52:01,485
Well, if it isn't the next
hospital director, Nicholas Tange.

857
00:52:04,020 --> 00:52:06,389
Thank you for employing Michiko Daimon.

858
00:52:07,457 --> 00:52:08,692
This is a melon.

859
00:52:14,731 --> 00:52:16,299
This is the bill.

860
00:52:20,070 --> 00:52:21,271
Get that.

861
00:52:22,105 --> 00:52:24,207
We have a bill for you as well.

862
00:52:24,841 --> 00:52:25,675
What?

863
00:52:26,042 --> 00:52:30,347
Dr. Daimon violated her contract
by disobeying the AI

864
00:52:30,413 --> 00:52:32,015
and conducted an operation
without permission.

865
00:52:32,415 --> 00:52:36,353
This is the operating room cost,
labor cost, medication cost,

866
00:52:36,419 --> 00:52:40,190
and contract violation fees
for what she did.

867
00:52:40,257 --> 00:52:41,691
TOTAL AMOUNT DUE

868
00:52:47,164 --> 00:52:48,298
I cannot pay this.

869
00:52:50,901 --> 00:52:54,304
Please accept this instead.

870
00:52:59,843 --> 00:53:01,978
I look forward to working
with you in the future.

871
00:53:02,846 --> 00:53:05,749
Please tell Dr. Daimon

872
00:53:07,450 --> 00:53:08,785
that I said that.

873
00:53:20,897 --> 00:53:22,365
Looking good.

874
00:53:22,933 --> 00:53:26,069
I really feel much better this time.

875
00:53:26,403 --> 00:53:28,138
Really? I'm glad to hear it.

876
00:53:28,572 --> 00:53:31,474
This is for you, Dr. Daimon.

877
00:53:31,541 --> 00:53:34,578
What's this? A boxed lunch? Are you sure?

878
00:53:34,678 --> 00:53:37,013
Take it. I know you're broke.

879
00:53:37,380 --> 00:53:39,683
I'm starving. Thank you.

880
00:53:40,817 --> 00:53:42,419
I'm so happy!

881
00:53:45,589 --> 00:53:46,590
Bye.

882
00:53:49,426 --> 00:53:52,462
When I was asleep during the operation,

883
00:53:53,830 --> 00:53:55,065
I felt

884
00:53:55,865 --> 00:53:58,201
someone lay their hand right here.

885
00:53:58,735 --> 00:54:01,304
You must have been dreaming of
the assistant director.

886
00:54:03,306 --> 00:54:05,008
It was a softer,

887
00:54:06,443 --> 00:54:08,812
warmer hand.

888
00:54:14,050 --> 00:54:17,420
That Nichotan is one heck of a cheat.

889
00:54:18,455 --> 00:54:19,623
What?

890
00:54:21,725 --> 00:54:23,193
I can't believe this.

891
00:54:25,095 --> 00:54:26,429
Akira!

892
00:54:26,830 --> 00:54:30,467
We have Rat Coin, right?

893
00:54:30,533 --> 00:54:33,503
- Rat Coin?
- That's right! Rat Coin!

894
00:54:33,570 --> 00:54:36,740
- We've got Rat Coin!
- That's right!

895
00:54:37,207 --> 00:54:38,908
Let's have a look at it, Michiko.

896
00:54:38,975 --> 00:54:40,010
Yes!

897
00:54:44,614 --> 00:54:46,049
RAT COIN FALLS DRASTICALLY

898
00:54:46,149 --> 00:54:47,550
FALLS DRASTICALLY

899
00:54:49,452 --> 00:54:50,620
No way!

900
00:54:52,255 --> 00:54:53,690
Really? It's going up again?

901
00:54:53,790 --> 00:54:55,458
It's fine! It's going great!

902
00:54:59,229 --> 00:55:01,364
Michiko, what's this?

903
00:55:02,265 --> 00:55:04,534
That's the boxed lunch
the cafeteria lady gave me.

904
00:55:04,634 --> 00:55:06,636
I waited so I could share it with you.

905
00:55:17,180 --> 00:55:19,749
- Does it look good?
- It looks great!

906
00:55:20,550 --> 00:55:23,453
She really saved up, didn't she?

907
00:55:23,820 --> 00:55:25,121
Michiko.

908
00:55:25,722 --> 00:55:28,725
The boxed lunch has all of my favorites.

909
00:55:28,825 --> 00:55:31,828
I'll make something
delicious for you, Michiko.

910
00:55:36,166 --> 00:55:37,534
Akira.

911
00:55:37,634 --> 00:55:39,636
I don't know what this is,
but it looks bad.

912
00:55:39,703 --> 00:55:41,371
<i>This is an illegitimate arrest!</i>

913
00:55:41,471 --> 00:55:43,340
<i>Get those mics out of my face!</i>

914
00:55:43,406 --> 00:55:44,541
<i>- Ebina!
- Yes, sir!</i>

915
00:55:44,641 --> 00:55:47,043
<i>This happened because of
your big blabbermouth!</i>

916
00:55:47,143 --> 00:55:48,244
What happened?

917
00:55:49,145 --> 00:55:49,979
Come to think of it,

918
00:55:50,046 --> 00:55:51,381
- I've barely seen this guy.
- I knew it.

919
00:55:51,448 --> 00:55:53,283
I was sure this kind of thing

920
00:55:53,350 --> 00:55:55,452
- would happen.
<i>- Don't show this on TV!</i>

921
00:55:55,552 --> 00:55:56,619
- Like what?
<i>- Hey!</i>

922
00:56:04,427 --> 00:56:05,662
Dr. Daimon.

923
00:56:06,896 --> 00:56:10,367
Won't you please forget about
what happened the other day?

924
00:56:11,568 --> 00:56:13,002
The cafeteria lady...

925
00:56:13,970 --> 00:56:16,873
looks a lot like my lover from long ago.

926
00:56:18,007 --> 00:56:21,578
During the surgery, I lost my temper.

927
00:56:23,046 --> 00:56:26,015
I am terribly sorry for my awful behavior.

928
00:56:26,649 --> 00:56:30,687
I can't believe I insulted
a friend such as you like that.

929
00:56:35,225 --> 00:56:36,226
"Friend"?

930
00:56:37,660 --> 00:56:41,464
As well as being a magnificent doctor,

931
00:56:42,432 --> 00:56:43,767
you're also an important friend.

932
00:56:44,734 --> 00:56:47,003
Thank you for saving Ichiko Iwata.

933
00:56:47,771 --> 00:56:50,373
We're going to celebrate her recovery now.

934
00:56:50,774 --> 00:56:51,908
Please join us.

935
00:56:51,975 --> 00:56:55,111
Let's celebrate our renewed
friendship over caipirinhas.

936
00:57:00,817 --> 00:57:02,051
I decline.

937
00:57:03,052 --> 00:57:04,187
It's a waste.

938
00:57:15,465 --> 00:57:17,333
<i>This woman hates groups,</i>

939
00:57:17,700 --> 00:57:21,571
<i>hates authority, and hates restrictions.</i>

940
00:57:22,005 --> 00:57:25,408
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

941
00:57:25,508 --> 00:57:26,910
<i>are her weapons.</i>

942
00:57:26,976 --> 00:57:29,679
We will now conduct
a pancreaticoduodenectomy.

943
00:57:29,779 --> 00:57:30,747
- Scalpel.
- Here.

944
00:57:32,315 --> 00:57:37,620
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,
otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

945
00:57:40,023 --> 00:57:42,725
<i>My life is worth 500 billion yen!</i>

946
00:57:42,826 --> 00:57:45,428
There's no way I'm giving
my liver to my father.

947
00:57:45,495 --> 00:57:48,131
<i>Are you abandoning the poor patients
in the group infirmary?</i>

948
00:57:48,198 --> 00:57:49,899
<i>I can't cause any more trouble
for the hospital.</i>

949
00:57:49,966 --> 00:57:51,100
I still want to marry Ken.

950
00:57:51,167 --> 00:57:53,369
I never fail.
